---
/**
 * en/about.astro | About, Data Sources & Legal Status
 */

export const prerender = true;

import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About & Data Sources" description="Information regarding official data sources, translation status, copyright (§ 5 UrhG), and digital accessibility on LawNetz.">
	<div class="content-container">
		<header class="content-header">
			<nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="breadcrumbs">
				<a href="/en">Home</a>
				<span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
				<span aria-current="page">About</span>
			</nav>

			<h1 class="content-title">About & Data Sources</h1>
			<p class="content-lead">Information on the official data sources, translation status, and accessibility of LawNetz.</p>
		</header>

		<div class="content-body">
			<section class="info-section">
				<h2>1. Official Data Source & Copyright Status</h2>
				<p>
					The statutes and regulations presented on this platform originate from the official repository of the <strong>Federal Ministry of Justice</strong> and the <strong>Federal Office of Justice</strong>, made accessible via <a href="https://www.gesetze-im-internet.de" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">gesetze-im-internet.de</a>.
				</p>
				<p>
					Pursuant to <strong>Section 5(1) of the German Act on Copyright and Related Rights (UrhG)</strong>, statutes, statutory instruments, official decrees and notices do not enjoy copyright protection. They are official works and are freely accessible to the public.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="info-section">
				<h2>2. Status of English Translations</h2>
				<p>
					The English translations available on LawNetz are produced by the Language Service of the Federal Ministry of Justice and commissioned translation services. They cover <strong>135 selected federal acts and regulations</strong> (such as the Civil Code, Criminal Code, Commercial Code, and Workplace Ordinance).
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>Important Legal Notice:</strong> These translations are provided solely for informational purposes and are non-official. In all cases, only the German versions promulgated in the Federal Law Gazette (Bundesgesetzblatt, BGBl.) are legally authoritative and binding.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section class="info-section">
				<h2>3. Digital Accessibility (WCAG 2.2 AAA)</h2>
				<p>LawNetz is built to adhere to the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG 2.2 Level AAA):</p>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Contrast Ratio:</strong> Text colors maintain a contrast ratio of at least 7:1 against backgrounds in both light and dark modes.</li>
					<li><strong>Keyboard Navigation:</strong> Sequential shortcuts (<kbd>g</kbd> followed by a destination key, or <kbd>?</kbd> for the shortcuts dialog), skip links, and ARIA landmarks.</li>
					<li><strong>Typography:</strong> Locally served fonts <em>Atkinson Hyperlegible</em> and <em>Lexend</em>.</li>
					<li><strong>Data Minimization:</strong> No tracking cookies, no third-party CDN requests, and client-side fulltext search.</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="info-section">
				<h2>4. Open Source</h2>
				<p>
					LawNetz is an independent open-source project. Source code, bug reports, and contributions are available on <a href="https://github.com/dstN/lawnetz.de" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>.
				</p>
			</section>
		</div>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.content-container {
		width: 100%;
		max-width: 100%;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		box-sizing: border-box;
	}

	.breadcrumbs {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: var(--space-2);
		font-size: var(--text-sm);
		color: var(--c-content-secondary);
		margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
	}

	.breadcrumbs a {
		color: var(--c-content-secondary);
		text-decoration: none;
	}

	.breadcrumbs a:hover {
		color: var(--c-primary);
		text-decoration: underline;
	}

	.content-header {
		margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--c-border);
		padding-bottom: var(--space-6);
	}

	.content-title {
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: var(--text-3xl);
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--c-content);
		line-height: var(--leading-tight);
		letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight);
		margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
	}

	@media (max-width: 860px) {
		.content-title {
			font-size: var(--text-2xl);
		}
	}

	.content-lead {
		font-size: var(--text-base);
		color: var(--c-content-secondary);
		line-height: var(--leading-normal);
	}

	.content-body {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: var(--space-8);
	}

	.info-section h2 {
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: var(--text-xl);
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--content-primary);
		margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
	}

	.info-section p {
		font-size: var(--text-base);
		color: var(--content-primary);
		line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
		margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
	}

	.info-section ul {
		list-style: disc;
		padding-left: var(--space-6);
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: var(--space-2);
		font-size: var(--text-base);
		color: var(--content-primary);
		line-height: var(--leading-normal);
	}

	.info-section a {
		color: var(--accent-default);
		text-decoration: underline;
	}

	kbd {
		display: inline-block;
		padding: 1px 5px;
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: var(--text-xs);
		background: var(--surface-sunken);
		border: 1px solid var(--border-default);
		border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
	}
</style>
